hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"148","As'alullāha ‘l-`Aẓīma Rabba ‘l-`Arshil-`Aẓīmi an yashfiyak. I ask Almighty Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to make you well. (Recite seven times in Arabic .) Reference: At-Tirmidhi, Abu Dawud. See also Al-Albani, Sahih At-Tirmidhi 2/210 and Sahihul-Jami' As-Saghir 5/180."
"149","Qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam: (Idhā ʿāda ar-rajulu akhāhu al-muslima, mashā fī khirāfati al-jannati ḥattā yajlisu, fa-idhā jalasa ghammarat-hu ar-raḥmah, fa-in kāna ghuṣwatan ṣallā ʿalayhi sabʿūna ʾalfa malikin ḥattā yumsī, wa-in kāna masāʾan ṣallā ʿalayhi sabʿūna ʾalfa malikin ḥattā yuṣbiḥ). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \When a man visits his Muslim brother (who is ill)"","" he walks through the gardens of Paradise until he sits down. When he sits"","" mercy overwhelms him. If he visits in the morning"","" seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening; and if he visits in the evening"","" seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning.\"""
